{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>For Haman son of Hammedatha.</b> The sense is: it is justice that they should accept this, for were it not for this deliverance, their name and the name of their seed would be blotted out, and they would commemorate it every year to give thanks to HaShem, to whom the plots were woven. The dagesh in the mem of להמם is for the loss of the doubling mem."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:22.705554871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}